  "summary": "Four NAR database updates pair expanded structural, ligand and interaction content with APIs, clients and agentic access, easing computational reuse.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is curated biomolecular resources expanding content while becoming easier to query programmatically. PDBe adds literature-mined residue annotations, MD simulation links via MDposit, MOLE pore analyses, and API and MCP agentic access. GPCRdb expands structure and ligand coverage, including Boltz-2 and AlphaFold2-Multimer models, with updated mapper and snakeplot visualizations. DGIdb adds new sources, Python and R client libraries, Docker images and versioned data releases. The Chemical Probes Portal reports 26% more curated probes and is expert-reviewed, so it fits this thread more loosely, as a curation resource rather than a structure-linked one. Predicted-structure content and machine-oriented interfaces are the new elements across these updates.",
